.Sh DESCRIPTION
These are the util-linux applets of BusyBox 1.36.1 as built for Rach2.
.Bl -tag -width scriptreplay
.It Nm blkid
Print file system UUIDs.
Read volumes through the disk nodes described in
.Xr disk 4 .
.It Nm cal
Display a calendar.
.It Nm chrt
Request a scheduling priority and class for a process.
The request fails with
.Er ENOSYS ,
as it does on Linux with the BusyBox of a musl system such as Alpine: musl,
unpatched as it is here, answers
.Fn sched_getscheduler ,
.Fn sched_setscheduler ,
.Fn sched_getparam
and
.Fn sched_setparam
itself, without the kernel, which has the calls
.Pq see Xr sched_setscheduler 2 .
.It Nm fallocate
Preallocate space for a file.
No file system here reserves space ahead of a write, so the request fails
with
.Er EOPNOTSUPP ,
as it does on Linux's ext2
.Pq see Xr fallocate 2 .
.It Nm fatattr
Change FAT file attributes.
Rach2 does not implement the FAT attribute requests, so the change fails.
.It Nm fbset
Show or modify frame buffer settings.
Rach2 has no
.Pa /dev/fb0
and does not implement the Linux frame buffer requests.
.It Nm fdflush
Request that a floppy drive detect a disk change.
Rach2 has no floppy devices and does not implement the request.
.It Nm fdformat
Format a floppy disk.
Rach2 has no floppy devices and does not implement the request.
.It Nm fdisk
Read or change a partition table.
Writing a table to a raw disk node requires the recovery kernel; an image
file can be written on any kernel.
.It Nm findfs
Find a file system device by label or UUID.
Read volumes through the disk nodes described in
.Xr disk 4 .
.It Nm flock
Request a lock or unlock on a file descriptor, or lock a file and run a program.
Rach2 registers no
.Fn flock
system call, so the request fails.
.It Nm freeramdisk
Request that all memory used by a RAM disk be freed.
Rach2 has no such device and does not implement the request.
.It Nm fsck.minix
Check a MINIX file system and optionally repair it.
.It Nm getopt
Parse command options for a shell script.
.It Nm hd
An alias for
.Ql hexdump -C .
.It Nm hexdump
Display files, or standard input, in a specified format.
.It Nm hwclock
Read the hardware real-time clock, set the system's time from it, or set it
from the system's, through
.Pa /dev/rtc0 ;
see
.Xr rtc 4 .
The clock keeps UTC, so
.Fl u
reads it as it is.
.It Nm ipcrm
Remove System V shared memory segments, message queues, or semaphores.
Rach2 has no System V IPC, so the applet fails.
.It Nm ipcs
Display System V shared memory, message queue, or semaphore information.
Rach2 has no System V IPC, so the applet fails.
.It Nm last
List the last users who logged in.
.It Nm linux32 , Nm linux64
Aliases for
.Ql setarch linux32
and
.Ql setarch linux64 .
.It Nm lspci
List PCI devices from
.Pa /sys/bus/pci/devices ,
by slot, class and IDs; see
.Xr sysfs 5 .
The kernel binds no driver a device's
.Pa uevent
names, so
.Fl k
adds nothing.
.It Nm lsusb
List the running USB devices from
.Pa /sys/bus/usb/devices ,
by bus, device number and IDs; see
.Xr sysfs 5 .
The root hubs are not listed.
.It Nm mesg
Control write access to the terminal.
The argument
.Cm y
allows access;
.Cm n
disallows it.
.It Nm mkdosfs , Nm mkfs.vfat
Create a FAT32 file system, which the kernel mounts as
.Cm vfat ,
in a partition node or a regular file.
.Ar KBYTES
gives the size and extends a file to it.
The ordinary kernel writes no disk node, so outside recovery the volume is
made in a file and mounted through a loop device; see
.Xr loopctl 8 .
.It Nm mkfs.minix
Create a MINIX file system.
.It Nm mkswap
Prepare a device as a swap partition.
Rach2 does not support swap.
.It Nm more
Display files, or standard input, one screen at a time.
.It Nm mount
Mount a file system; see
.Xr mount 8 .
File system autodetection requires
.Pa /proc .
.It Nm mountpoint
Check whether a directory is a mount point.
.It Nm nologin
Refuse a login.
.It Nm nsenter
Request entry into namespaces and run a program.
Rach2 has no namespaces, so the request fails.
.It Nm pivot_root
Request that the current root file system be moved to
.Ar PUT_OLD
and
.Ar NEW_ROOT
be made the root file system.
Rach2 does not implement the call, so the request fails.
.It Nm rdate
Print, or attempt to set, the time from
.Ar HOST
using RFC 868.
Rach2 has no
.Fn settimeofday
handler, so setting the clock fails;
.Fl p
prints the remote time.
.It Nm rdev
Print the device node for the file system mounted at
.Pa / .
.It Nm readprofile
Read kernel profiling counters from
.Pa /proc/profile ,
which Rach2 does not have.
.It Nm renice
Request a change to a running process's scheduling priority.
Rach2 does not implement the priority calls, so the request fails.
.It Nm rev
Reverse the characters in each line of a file.
.It Nm rtcwake
Request a system sleep state until a specified wakeup time.
Rach2 has neither the RTC nor the suspend interfaces it uses.
.It Nm script
Record a terminal session in
.Ar OUTFILE ,
which defaults to
.Pa typescript .
.It Nm scriptreplay
Play back a terminal session using its timing information.
.It Nm setarch
Run a program with the selected uname emulation:
.Cm linux32
for 32 bits or
.Cm linux64
for 64 bits.
Rach2 does not implement the personality call, so the request fails.
.It Nm setsid
Run a program in a new session.
Without
.Fl c ,
the program has no controlling terminal and keyboard signals such as
Ctrl-C do not affect it.
.It Nm swapoff , Nm swapon
Request that swapping on a device stop or start, respectively.
Rach2 does not support swap.
.It Nm taskset
Set or get CPU affinity.
Rach2 does not implement the affinity calls, so the applet fails.
.It Nm umount
Unmount file systems; see
.Xr mount 8 .
.It Nm unshare
Request separate namespaces for a program.
Rach2 has no namespaces, so the request fails.
.It Nm xxd
Display a hexadecimal dump of a file or standard input.
.El
.Pp
The
.Nm losetup
applet is not built.
Use
.Xr loopctl 8
to configure Rach2 loop devices.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Ss cal
.Bl -tag -width "-j"
.It Fl j
Use Julian dates.
.It Fl m
Start the week on Monday.
.It Fl y
Display the whole year.
.El
.Ss chrt
.Bl -tag -width "-p"
.It Fl m
Show minimum and maximum priorities.
.It Fl p
Operate on
.Ar PID .
.It Fl r
Select SCHED_RR.
.It Fl f
Select SCHED_FIFO.
.It Fl o
Select SCHED_OTHER.
.It Fl b
Select SCHED_BATCH.
.It Fl i
Select SCHED_IDLE.
.El
.Ss fatattr
Prefix attributes with
.Ql -
to clear them or
.Ql +
to set them.
The attributes are:
.Bl -tag -width r -compact
.It Cm r
Read only.
.It Cm h
Hidden.
.It Cm s
System.
.It Cm v
Volume label.
.It Cm d
Directory.
.It Cm a
Archive.
.El
.Ss fdformat
.Fl n
omits verification after formatting.
.Ss fdisk
.Bl -tag -width "-C CYLINDERS"
.It Fl u
Display start and end positions in sectors instead of cylinders.
.It Fl l
Display each disk's partition table and exit.
.It Fl b Ar SSZ
Select the sector size;
.Fl b Cm 2048
selects 2048-byte sectors for certain magneto-optical disks.
.It Fl C Ar CYLINDERS
Set the cylinder count.
.It Fl H Ar HEADS
Set the head count, typically 255.
.It Fl S Ar SECTORS
Set the sector count, typically 63.
.El
.Ss flock
.Bl -tag -width "-x"
.It Fl s
Request a shared lock.
.It Fl x
Request an exclusive lock; this is the default.
.It Fl u
Unlock the file descriptor.
.It Fl n
Fail instead of waiting for a lock.
.El
.Ss fsck.minix
.Bl -tag -width "-l"
.It Fl l
List all file names.
.It Fl a
Repair automatically.
.It Fl r
Repair interactively.
.It Fl v
Produce verbose output.
.It Fl s
Print superblock information.
.It Fl m
Show
.Ql mode not cleared
warnings.
.It Fl f
Force a file system check.
.El
.Ss getopt
.Bl -tag -width "-o OPTSTRING"
.It Fl a
Allow long options beginning with a single hyphen.
.It Fl l Ar LOPT Ns Op ,...
Specify the long options to recognize.
.It Fl n Ar PROGNAME
Use this program name in error messages.
.It Fl o Ar OPTSTRING
Specify the short options to recognize.
.It Fl q
Suppress error messages for unrecognized options.
.It Fl Q
Suppress normal output.
.It Fl s Ar SHELL
Select shell quoting conventions.
.It Fl T
Test the version; exit with status 4.
.It Fl u
Do not quote output.
.El
.Ss hexdump
.Bl -tag -width "-f FMT_FILE"
.It Fl b
Display bytes in octal.
.It Fl c
Display bytes as characters.
.It Fl d
Display two-byte units in decimal.
.It Fl o
Display two-byte units in octal.
.It Fl x
Display two-byte units in hexadecimal.
.It Fl C
Display hexadecimal and ASCII, 16 bytes per line.
.It Fl v
Display all input without folding duplicate lines.
.It Fl e Ar FMT
Use the format string, for example:
.Dl '16/1 \(dq%02x|\(dq\(dq\en\(dq'
.It Fl f Ar FMT_FILE
Read the format from a file.
.El
.Ss ipcrm
Uppercase options select an object by key; lowercase options select it by ID.
.Bl -tag -width "-m, -M"
.It Fl m , Fl M
Remove a shared memory segment after the last detach.
.It Fl q , Fl Q
Remove a message queue.
.It Fl s , Fl S
Remove a semaphore.
.El
.Ss ipcs
.Bl -tag -width "-i ID"
.It Fl i Ar ID
Show a specific resource.
.It Fl m
Show shared memory segments.
.It Fl q
Show message queues.
.It Fl s
Show semaphore arrays.
.It Fl a
Show all resources; this is the default.
.It Fl t
Show times.
.It Fl c
Show creators.
.It Fl p
Show process IDs.
.It Fl l
Show limits.
.It Fl u
Show a summary.
.El
.Ss lspci
.Fl m
selects parsable output;
.Fl k
shows the driver.
.Ss mkdosfs, mkfs.vfat
.Bl -tag -width "-n LABEL"
.It Fl n Ar LABEL
Set the volume label.
.It Fl v
Print the layout.
.El
.Ss mkfs.minix
.Bl -tag -width "-i INODES"
.It Fl c
Check for bad blocks.
.It Fl l Ar FILE
Read the bad block list from a file.
.It Fl n Ar XX
Set the maximum file name length to 14 or 30.
.It Fl i Ar XX
Set the inode count.
.It Fl v
Create a version 2 file system.
.El
.Ss mkswap
.Fl L Ar LBL
sets the label.
.Ss mount
.Bl -tag -width "-a"
.It Fl a
Mount all file systems in fstab.
.It Fl f
Perform a dry run.
.It Fl v
Produce verbose output.
.El
.Pp
See
.Xr mount 8
for Rach2 mount options and restrictions.
.Ss mountpoint
.Bl -tag -width "-x DEVICE"
.It Fl q
Suppress output.
.It Fl d
Print the file system's major and minor device numbers.
.It Fl n
Print the file system's device name.
.El
.Ss nsenter
.Bl -tag -width "--preserve-credentials"
.It Fl t Ar PID
Get namespaces from the target process.
.It Fl m Ns Op Ar FILE
Enter the mount namespace.
.It Fl u Ns Op Ar FILE
Enter the UTS namespace, which includes the host name.
.It Fl i Ns Op Ar FILE
Enter the System V IPC namespace.
.It Fl n Ns Op Ar FILE
Enter the network namespace.
.It Fl p Ns Op Ar FILE
Enter the process ID namespace.
.It Fl U Ns Op Ar FILE
Enter the user namespace.
.It Fl S Ar UID
Set the user ID in the entered namespace.
.It Fl G Ar GID
Set the group ID in the entered namespace.
.It Fl -preserve-credentials
Leave user and group IDs unchanged.
.It Fl r Ns Op Ar DIR
Set the root directory.
.It Fl w Ns Op Ar DIR
Set the working directory.
.It Fl F
Do not fork before executing the program.
.El
.Ss rdate
.Fl s
only sets the system time, which fails on Rach2;
.Fl p
only prints the time.
.Ss readprofile
.Bl -tag -width "-p PROFILE"
.It Fl m Ar MAPFILE
Select the map file; the default is
.Pa /boot/System.map .
.It Fl p Ar PROFILE
Select the profile file; the default is
.Pa /proc/profile .
.It Fl M Ar NUM
Set the profiling multiplier.
.It Fl i
Print only information about the sampling step.
.It Fl v
Produce verbose output.
.It Fl a
Print all symbols, including those with zero counts.
.It Fl b
Print individual histogram bin counts.
.It Fl s
Print individual counters within functions.
.It Fl r
Reset all counters; requires root.
.It Fl n
Disable byte order autodetection.
.El
.Ss renice
.Bl -tag -width "-n"
.It Fl n
Add
.Ar PRIORITY
to the current nice value.
Without this option, set the nice value to
.Ar PRIORITY .
.It Fl p
Interpret IDs as process IDs; this is the default.
.It Fl g
Interpret IDs as process group IDs.
.It Fl u
Interpret IDs as user names.
.El
.Ss rtcwake
.Bl -tag -width "-m MODE"
.It Fl a
Read the clock mode from
.Pa /etc/adjtime ;
this is the default.
.It Fl l
Treat the RTC as local time.
.It Fl u
Treat the RTC as UTC.
.It Fl d Ar DEV
Select the RTC device.
.It Fl m Ar MODE
Select the sleep state; the default is
.Cm standby .
.It Fl s Ar SEC
Set the wakeup time to this many seconds from now.
.It Fl t Ar TIME
Set the wakeup time in seconds since the epoch.
.El
.Ss script
.Bl -tag -width "-t[FILE]"
.It Fl a
Append output.
.It Fl c Ar PROG
Run the program instead of the shell.
.El
.Ss setarch , linux32 , linux64
.Fl R
requests that address space randomization be disabled.
.Ss setsid
.Fl c
sets the controlling terminal to standard input.
.Ss swapoff
.Fl a
requests that swapping stop on all swap devices.
.Ss swapon
.Bl -tag -width "-d[POL]"
.It Fl a
Start swapping on all swap devices.
.It Fl e
Silently skip devices that do not exist.
.It Fl d Ns Op Ar POL
Discard blocks when swapping starts if
.Ar POL
is
.Cm once ,
when blocks are freed if it is
.Cm pages ,
or at both times if omitted.
.It Fl p Ar PRI
Set the swap device priority.
.El
.Ss taskset
.Bl -tag -width "-c LIST"
.It Fl p
Operate on
.Ar PID .
.It Fl a
Operate on all threads.
.It Fl c Ar LIST
Specify affinity as a list instead of a hexadecimal mask.
.El
.Ss umount
.Bl -tag -width "-t FSTYPE[,...]"
.It Fl a
Unmount all file systems.
.It Fl r
Remount read-only if the device is busy.
.It Fl l
Request a lazy unmount, detaching the file system.
.It Fl f
Force an unmount, for example for an unreachable NFS server.
.It Fl t Ar FSTYPE Ns Op ,...
Unmount only the specified file system types.
.El
.Pp
See
.Xr mount 8
for Rach2 unmount restrictions.
.Ss unshare
.Bl -tag -width "--propagation MODE"
.It Fl m , Fl -mount Ns Op = Ns Ar FILE
Unshare the mount namespace.
.It Fl u , Fl -uts Ns Op = Ns Ar FILE
Unshare the UTS namespace, which includes the host name.
.It Fl i , Fl -ipc Ns Op = Ns Ar FILE
Unshare the System V IPC namespace.
.It Fl n , Fl -net Ns Op = Ns Ar FILE
Unshare the network namespace.
.It Fl p , Fl -pid Ns Op = Ns Ar FILE
Unshare the process ID namespace.
.It Fl U , Fl -user Ns Op = Ns Ar FILE
Unshare the user namespace.
.It Fl f
Fork before executing the program.
.It Fl r
Map the current user to root; implies
.Fl U .
.It Fl -mount-proc Ns Op = Ns Ar DIR
Mount
.Pa /proc
first; implies
.Fl m .
.It Fl -propagation Ar MODE
Set mount propagation to
.Cm slave , shared , private ,
or
.Cm unchanged .
.It Fl -setgroups Cm allow Ns | Ns Cm deny
Control the setgroups system call in user namespaces.
.El
.Ss xxd
.Bl -tag -width "-l LEN"
.It Fl g Ar N
Set the bytes per group.
.It Fl c Ar N
Set the bytes per line.
.It Fl p
Print only hexadecimal bytes; assumes
.Fl c Ns Cm 30 .
.It Fl i
Use C include file format.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /boot/System.map
.It Pa /boot/System.map
Default map file for
.Nm readprofile .
.It Pa /proc/profile
Default profile file for
.Nm readprofile .
.It Pa /etc/adjtime
Default clock mode file for
.Nm rtcwake .
.It Pa typescript
Default output file for
.Nm script .
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Read kernel messages one screen at a time:
.Dl dmesg | more
.Pp
Find a device by its file system label:
.Dl findfs LABEL=MyDevice
